<svelte:head><title>Help — WantMyTime</title></svelte:head>
<section class="article-page">
	<p class="eyebrow">Help</p>
	<h1 class="page-heading">Straight answers.</h1>
	<div class="faq">
		<details><summary>Who is WantMyTime for?</summary><p>Anyone people keep asking for time: consultants, doctors, lawyers, founders, creators, coaches, mentors. If people want your advice, your attention or an hour of your day, you can put a price on it.</p></details>
		<details><summary>Can I charge friends too?</summary><p>Your link, your call. Send it to whoever you like. If you’d rather give someone your time free, just don’t send them the link.</p></details>
		<details><summary>What does it cost?</summary><p>Nothing to set up. We keep 5% of each paid booking. The person booking pays the bank transfer fee on top of your price, so your 95% is never touched.</p></details>
		<details><summary>How do people pay me?</summary><p>By bank transfer. At checkout they get an account number for that booking only, send the exact amount from any Nigerian bank app, and the booking confirms itself once the money arrives.</p></details>
		<details><summary>When does the money reach my bank?</summary><p>About three hours after each call ends. We hold the payment until the call is over and the two hours the buyer has to report a problem have passed, then send your share to the bank account you added under Settings → Payouts. Most banks show it within minutes.</p></details>
		<details><summary>Does the person booking need an account?</summary><p>No. They type their name and email, then pay. That’s it.</p></details>
		<details><summary>Where does the call happen?</summary><p>Wherever you like. Connect Google Calendar and each booking gets its own Google Meet link automatically, or paste any meeting link on the booking.</p></details>
		<details><summary>What if they don’t show up?</summary><p>Report it from the booking page after the start time. If the buyer didn’t come, you’re still paid. If you didn’t come, the buyer is refunded in full.</p></details>
		<details><summary>What if I need to cancel or move a booking?</summary><p>Either of you can suggest a new time from the booking page; nothing changes until the other person accepts. If you cancel, the buyer gets everything back. If they cancel, your cancellation policy decides the refund.</p></details>
		<details><summary>Can I take a break?</summary><p>Yes. Pause new bookings from Your link, or close particular dates under Availability. Bookings you already have stay in place.</p></details>
		<details><summary>Something went wrong. What now?</summary><p>Report it from your booking page within two hours of the call ending. The payout waits while we look at it, and we can refund part or all of the payment.</p></details>
	</div>
</section>
